      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, my goal is a workflow similar to `repo sync` where everything involved is fetched before any other work begins (merging in this case); that way, there\u0027s not even a need to be online.\n\nIt seems the only way to get the desired commit message in this situation is to fake it. That\u0027s fine, and it\u0027s not hard to [automate](https://codeberg.org/t-m-w/porting_scripts/src/branch/main/qcom-merge.sh) [that](https://codeberg.org/t-m-w/porting_scripts/src/commit/4d63d1bec0e833af237b38c36dc4c53b8adc85f5/qcom-merge.sh#L248), so that\u0027s what I\u0027m doing for the title, but you can see it still says \"* tag \u0027clo/display-drivers/LA.UM.9.14.r1-26000-LAHAINA.QSSI15.0\u0027\" later in the message. Resolving that requires fancier faking, like writing into `FETCH_HEAD` myself and merging that.\n\nIs it worth it, or is it fine enough having the actual tag and URL in the commit title?",
